title: 'statement-store: source the bloom false-positive rate and seed from CLI'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    Two hidden CLI flags on the substrate node and omni-node set the parameters
    of the topic-affinity bloom filter advertised on the v2 DHT statement path:
    `--statement-bloom-false-positive-rate` and `--statement-bloom-seed`. The
    seed defaults to a random value per node, as before. The default
    false-positive rate drops from 0.01 to 0.001, which also serves as the
    accepted minimum: lower rates would push the filter past the wire limits
    peers enforce at decode.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `sc_statement_store::Config` gains `bloom_false_pos_rate` and `bloom_seed`,
    checked by `Config::validate` against `DEFAULT_BLOOM_FALSE_POS_RATE` as the
    floor. `StatementHandlerPrototype::build` takes both values as new
    arguments and passes them to `ExplicitAffinity`.
crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: major
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: minor
- name: staging-node-cli
  bump: minor
